{"version":1,"vintage":{"installations":"Directory of Federal Real Property, as retrieved","census":"2021 Census"},"sources":["tbs_dfrp","statcan_military"],"rule":"A city gets an Encampment when (a) a Canadian Forces base of tier 'major' or 'base' lies in it (within 5 km of its boundary), and (b) residents serving in the Canadian Armed Forces (2021 Census, table 98-10-0142, where they live) are at least 1% of residents 17 and over, or at least 2,000 and at least 0.3%. Tier: 'fortress' at 3% or more, otherwise 'garrison'. 'naval' when its Navy bases outweigh its Army and Air Force ones, counting a 'major' base as 4 and a 'base' as 1 (the U.S. rule).","rules":{"tier":"No per-base headcount is published, so size comes from land area, as in the U.S.: 'major' = a base of at least 100 km² (its satellite properties folded in), or one of this project's flagships on small land (CFB Halifax, CFB Esquimalt, CFB Edmonton, CFB Kingston, CFB Borden, CFB Cold Lake, CFB Trenton, CFB Winnipeg: the fleet bases, division and air division headquarters, the main training base, and the main fighter and air mobility wings; flagged curated); 'base' = at least 1 km²; 'site' = the rest. The bases are a hand-checked list of the Canadian Forces' main bases, wings and stations, not every DND property.","ranges":"Every DND military property of 100 km² or more (the Cold Lake Air Weapons Range's Alberta and Saskatchewan halves as one). DND publishes no boundaries, so each is drawn on the hexes of its parcel points, not its full extent.","encampment":"A city gets an Encampment when (a) a Canadian Forces base of tier 'major' or 'base' lies in it (within 5 km of its boundary), and (b) residents serving in the Canadian Armed Forces (2021 Census, table 98-10-0142, where they live) are at least 1% of residents 17 and over, or at least 2,000 and at least 0.3%. Tier: 'fortress' at 3% or more, otherwise 'garrison'. 'naval' when its Navy bases outweigh its Army and Air Force ones, counting a 'major' base a